  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 155 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nSunday and Monday will be very similar to the last few days with \nhighs in the 90s to around 100F for most and isolated storms over \nthe higher terrain. Heading into the middle of the coming week, the \nridge that has been meandering across the US will flatten out over \nthe southeastern US and the Gulf. This will not change temperatures \nmuch as highs will remain above normal in the upper 90s to low 100s \nfor most. It will dry the region out and push rain chances to below \n5% each day. Continued southerly/southeasterly flow persists and \nthat may lead to a storm or two developing in the vicinity of any of \nthe mountainous zones in the area. Overnight lows in the 60s to 70s \ncan be expected each night through the extended. \n\n-Stickney",
